{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:39:53.867770Z","id":"e04b8c11caf126353cf9d2f79d36927d8b8a56c066277f04807dd8f64de7eb35","body":{"detail":"Background.swift has no unit test target: margin, ackWait, tick and remaining are stored properties a test could set, but no ios_unit_test exists. The simulator showed only the trim on leaving (os_log 'Clax trim began' / 'Clax trim ended', and 'trimmed memory' in daemon.log) and the trim on a memory warning (written to <device>/data/var/run/memory_warning_simulation). No caller sends pauseDone yet (lib/platform/background_work.dart IosBackgroundWork.pauseDone has no caller in lib/), so every pause waits the full ackWait before trimming.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":120},"end":{"line":174},"content_hash":"ab367a42378343bb7f18d635c145567a5ad05658a8820f689412366279a55653"},"suggested_fix":"Drive the DEBUG expireBackgroundTask hook from a simulator integration test with a run recorded, and check the 'Clax run pausing' / 'Clax run paused' / 'Clax run ended' lines and the stopped call in Dart.","summary":"The pause path (the 5 s margin, the expiration handler, the 2 s wait for pauseDone, then trim and end) has no automated test","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T06:59:02.421779Z","id":"32f8b7a302b21c9c51f8acc381846117ae0594eb687cf6a634ceaea595bdd921","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"e04b8c11caf126353cf9d2f79d36927d8b8a56c066277f04807dd8f64de7eb35","summary":"pauseDone now has a caller: AppRoot._pauseRuns (apps/clax_app/lib/app.dart) sends it after AppPresence.pause and the paused notice (test/app_background_test.dart 'on iOS the change is paused with one notice, then pauseDone; ...'). The Swift pause path itself is still untested, so this stays open.","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:17:32.807501Z","id":"94d49a112c5d373248c6f6098e732f6bc91f5e2873fbde918cc26acf28e72dc6","body":{"detail":"The manifest declares one collected data type, NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypeOtherUserContent (linked false, tracking false, purpose AppFunctionality), as docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-18-ios-release-design.md §10.4 drafts it: what the person types or says, and their app's code, go to Anthropic's Claude API under the person's own API key; Clax's developer receives nothing. The spec's open question 7 (same file, 'The privacy label (blocks external TestFlight)') asks the owner to confirm this reading. Options: (a) keep it; (b) declare nothing collected, on the reading that data sent to a third party under the person's own key at their request is not collected by the developer; (c) another type or purpose. The App Store Connect privacy label must agree with whatever is chosen. apps/clax_app/tool/ios-app-check.sh asserts the current entry field by field, so a change edits both.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":27},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"b6136698b4103ce8c2abcc14fed4ab3e51a0aabe801bd536b30ef32f251edf35"},"summary":"Owner decision: are the person's requests and app code, sent to Anthropic under the person's own key, 'Other User Content' for App Functionality, not linked, not tracking?","tags":["status:needs-decision","ios","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/PrivacyInfo.xcprivacy","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:17:32.807581Z","id":"a6b7dd3d8e97f5b1a50791400396c43e20165e7f0a9886aeba33021952ee1212","body":{"detail":"nm -u on the simulator Clax.app/Clax imports _statfs and _fstatfs; in libclax_ios.a only the libsqlite3-sys object imports them. libsqlite3-sys 0.30.1's sqlite3.c (unixOpen, around line 44826) calls fstatfs to compare f_fstypename with msdos/exfat, and statfs in its locking-style and proxy paths. None of Apple's DiskSpace reasons (85F4.1, E174.1, 7D9E.1, B728.1) describes a file-system type check; E174.1 is the nearest, since the check precedes writes to the database. App Store review accepts or rejects the reason; ios-app-check.sh fails if a DiskSpace symbol disappears from or appears in the binary without the manifest following.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":52},"end":{"line":59},"content_hash":"0e5d12db64042e414672c08ad84cd1cd937408ebc7c0543a266c9b0a30b88b0c"},"summary":"DiskSpace is declared with E174.1 (free space before a write), but the binary's only statfs/fstatfs caller, SQLite, reads the file system's type, not its free space","tags":["ios","privacy","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:26:08.477411Z","id":"57990157e76d09bb78cfaac2779dc1785eb5f353382172015aa57086664a3cfe","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:integration_ios_pause calls Background.expire() through the test channel (ios/Runner/TestChannel.swift), which runs pause(force: true): it checks that 'stopped' reaches Dart, one paused notice is delivered and the scripted run is held until Clax is back. beginRun's Timer comparing remaining() with margin, and the beginBackgroundTask expiration handler, are never run by a test; nor is the end of the held task after pauseDone (trim, then endRun), which Dart cannot observe. A wrong margin comparison or an expiration handler that never fires would pass every test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":125},"end":{"line":149},"content_hash":"1f6b609b8c3a418782f66e4fbe1f5348ab1a37e22a167a2f77d5647ac361bfaa"},"suggested_fix":"Give the test channel a way to set Background.shared's margin and remaining (both stored properties) so a simulator test can pass the margin without expire(), and have TestChannel answer whether a 'Clax run' task is held, so the test can check it ends after pauseDone.","summary":"The two automatic pause triggers, the 5 s margin timer and the 'Clax run' expiration handler, have no automated test: the simulator test drives only the DEBUG expire() path","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:26:17.113224Z","id":"4d19c9fa25ed74743daa56cbd06814320caec6115f25af447cd5e799d7508a5c","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Fixed for the pause path: //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_pause passes 3 of 3 runs on Clax iPhone (bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_pause --runs_per_test=3): Background.expire() through the test channel calls 'stopped', Dart pauses the runs, one paused notice is delivered and pauseDone is sent, and the run resumes when Clax is back. The margin timer and the expiration handler, which no test drives, are recorded in 57990157.","supersedes":"e04b8c11caf126353cf9d2f79d36927d8b8a56c066277f04807dd8f64de7eb35","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T09:39:08.878052Z","id":"a4bf00727e8a85e7a023542c2fc50e0e8b26731d22fb87d5832960074893b4ad","body":{"detail":"//apps/clax_app:ios_app_test builds the simulator app with this file and the patched webview_flutter_wkwebview; the isolation spike (integration_test/scheme_spike.dart) runs only on the Mac (integration_scheme_spike) and the Android emulator (integration_android_scheme_spike). An integration_test/ios_scheme_spike_test.dart would run it on Clax iPhone.","kind":"concern","summary":"The scheme host on iOS is built but not run: no spike runs on the simulator","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T10:18:26.371015Z","id":"e930537e666bacd45918d26abe01755f7692eb81f669bfdea01c430505b22a93","body":{"detail":"Runnable as is: an integration_test/ios_scheme_spike_test.dart (runSpike, printSpikeReport, expectIsolated, then the iOS rig's teardown: pumpWidget(SizedBox()) and semanticsEnabledTestValue = false, as integration_test/ios_rig.dart:456-463 does) is picked up by clax_ios_integration_tests (bazel/flutter/ios.bzl:211) as //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_scheme_spike. Run on 2026-10-20 on Clax iPhone: PASSED in 21.7s (CLAX_INTEGRATION_RESULT=0). Without the teardown it fails on 'A SemanticsHandle was active at the end of the test'. The simulator console the runner reads (tool/ios-integration-run.sh) does not show the spike's debugPrint lines, so which race branch it took is not visible; the file is not committed.","kind":"comment","references":"a4bf00727e8a85e7a023542c2fc50e0e8b26731d22fb87d5832960074893b4ad","summary":"The spike runs and passes on the simulator through the existing iOS integration path once an ios_scheme_spike_test.dart with the iOS rig's semantics teardown exists","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/SchemeHost.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T12:34:44.277330Z","id":"231f6681359d291e76dc47cdc46fefb7144780dd76e381e34f41aba7413ecdf1","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"Done in f1c07f346b12 as the reply e930537e describes: integration_test/ios_scheme_spike_test.dart runs runSpike, printSpikeReport and expectIsolated on Clax iPhone, ending with the iOS rig's teardown. bazelisk test //apps/clax_app:integration_ios_scheme_spike on 2026-10-20 with f1c07f346b12's SchemeHost.swift: PASSED in 23.4s (CLAX_INTEGRATION_RESULT=0).","supersedes":"a4bf00727e8a85e7a023542c2fc50e0e8b26731d22fb87d5832960074893b4ad","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T18:17:18.004379Z","id":"778a11671219d65bbb01264d855749ad5e7afa97ab61d54ab302b9de4610b54a","body":{"detail":"trimCore invokes 'trim' on dev.empathic.clax/background and runs done on any answer. IosBackgroundWork._onCall (lib/platform/background_work.dart) answers every method but 'stopped' with null at once, so leaving the app, a pause and a memory warning end their tasks without trimming the core's memory or checkpointing its WAL until that handler awaits CoreHost.trim() (POST /api/core/trim). A Dart handler that never answers holds the 'Clax trim' task until its expiration handler. No simulator test drives 'trim' (integration_test/ios_background_test.dart does not).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":195},"end":{"line":197},"content_hash":"e6dae714bc9a0f99a0a27369f6e9be34da2ae1c61be463a80dfcd810bc354c46"},"summary":"The iOS trims now wait on Dart's answer to 'trim': until the Dart side calls POST /api/core/trim for it, iOS suspends the app with no trim or checkpoint","tags":["core","ios","background","unverified","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"apps/clax_app/ios/Runner/Background.swift","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-20T21:29:58.792540Z","id":"a4c1305447a9e1cedcedca856bc844b2a72c004c980b2b2fa345fd11e60e19a8","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:f1c07f346b12","summary":"IosBackgroundWork answers 'trim' once its onTrim (CoreHost.trim, POST /api/core/trim; lib/main.dart) completes. Evidence: //apps/clax_app:platform_background_work_test PASSED, 'trim from the native side is answered once the core trimmed', which fails with the call left unawaited or the 'trim' case removed.","supersedes":"778a11671219d65bbb01264d855749ad5e7afa97ab61d54ab302b9de4610b54a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
